{
  "Answer": {
    "Title": "Deploy Job Missing Production Branch Filter",
    "Explanation": [
      "The workflow ran on branch `koans-08-branch-filters` and every job, including `deploy`, completed successfully — so the pipeline is green (all jobs SUCCESS, workflow SUCCESS). However, the stated requirement is that `deploy` should only ever run on commits to the `production` branch. The config contains no `filters` stanza at all, so `deploy` runs on every branch; the workflow log confirms it executed on a feature branch. Therefore the observed behaviour does not match the requirement. The correct fix is to attach a branch filter to the `deploy` job's entry in the workflow (filters are honoured at the workflow job-invocation level in 2.1 workflows, not in the job definition), whitelisting only `production`:",
      "",
      "```yaml",
      "      - deploy:",
      "          requires:",
      "            - test-production",
      "          filters:",
      "            branches:",
      "              only: production",
      "```",
      "",
      "Using `only: production` is preferable to an `ignore` list because it guarantees no other branch can ever trigger a deploy. Relying on `requires` alone does not help, since `requires` only controls ordering/dependencies, not which branches the job runs on."
    ],
    "ActualAnswer": [
      "{",
      "  \"behaviour_correct\": false,",
      "  \"fix\": \"filters_branches_only_production\",",
      "  \"fix_target_job\": \"deploy\",",
      "  \"pipeline_green\": true",
      "}"
    ],
    "ExpectedAnswer": [
