    "Title": "Missing app paths in persist_to_workspace caused deploy failure",
    "Explanation": [
      "The three build jobs each create their app file under app/\u003cplatform\u003e/ but only persist the meta/\u003cplatform\u003e directories to the workspace. The workflow summary shows all three build jobs SUCCESS (they only echo/mkdir and persist meta, nothing fails), while deploy FAILED. The deploy log confirms the attached workspace contained only ./meta/linux/build.txt, ./meta/mac/build.txt, ./meta/windows/build.txt — no app files — so the `test -f app/linux/app.linux` assertion exited 1. Therefore builds_green=true, deploy_green=false, workspace_had_apps=false. The correct fix is to add the app/\u003cplatform\u003e directories to the persist_to_workspace paths in each build job (persist_app_paths), so the generated app files reach deploy for store_artifacts. Merely changing the attach path, removing the verification, storing artifacts in the build jobs instead, or fixing only one platform would not satisfy the requirement that all three apps be persisted to deploy and uploaded there."
