{
  "Answer": {
    "Title": "Deploy Job Missing Tag Filter for Beta",
    "Explanation": [
      "The workflow_2.txt log shows the 'build-test-and-deploy' pipeline finished with a SUCCESS status (green pipeline) — build, test, and deploy jobs all passed. However, examining the trigger details, this pipeline was triggered from a branch commit (branch: koans-09-tag-filters) via the API, NOT from a tagged commit. Despite this, the 'deploy' job still ran and succeeded. This violates the stated requirement that deploy should ONLY run for tags matching the beta pattern (e.g., 'beta-main-0.1.1') and must NOT run for branch commits or alpha- tags. Looking at config_7.yml, the deploy job has no 'filters' key at all under the workflow definition — it only has a 'requires' clause on 'test'. In CircleCI, by default, jobs run on every branch push, and are excluded from tag-triggered pipelines unless an explicit 'filters.tags' block is added. Since no filters exist here, the deploy job runs on all branch commits (as evidenced in the log) and would not even run correctly for tags without an explicit tags filter. Therefore, although the pipeline result is green, the underlying behavior is incorrect: deploy is running on branch commits when it should be restricted solely to beta-* tagged commits. To fix this, the deploy job needs a 'filters' block specifying 'tags: only: /^beta-.*/' to allow tag-triggered runs matching the beta naming scheme, combined with 'branches: ignore: /.*/' to prevent it from running on any branch commit. This corresponds to the fix category 'filters_tags_only_beta', targeting the 'deploy' job specifically (build and test are unaffected by this requirement and should continue running on every commit as before)."
    ],
    "ActualAnswer": [
      "{",
      "  \"behaviour_correct\": false,",
      "  \"fix\": \"filters_tags_only_beta\",",
      "  \"fix_target_job\": \"deploy\",",
      "  \"pipeline_green\": true",
      "}"
    ],
    "ExpectedAnswer": [
      [
        "{",
        "  \"behaviour_correct\": false,",
        "  \"fix\": \"filters_tags_only_beta\",",
        "  \"fix_target_job\": \"all_jobs\",",
