    "Explanation": [
      "Goal: ensure the deploy job runs only when the commit is a tag that matches the beta product naming (examples: \"beta-main-0.1.1\") and does not run for alpha- tags or normal branch commits. CircleCI workflows support per-job filters that can restrict runs to branches and tags. To accomplish this, add a filters block under the deploy job in the workflow and use the tags: only key with a regular expression that matches the desired tag pattern. Using a regex anchored at the start (^) ensures tags that begin with \"beta-\" are allowed; alpha- tags and branch commits will not match and therefore the deploy job will be skipped. I verified the rest of the workflow dependencies stay the same (deploy requires test), so the pipeline stays green when deploy is allowed and deploy will be skipped otherwise. Example change: under workflows -\u003e build-test-and-deploy -\u003e jobs -\u003e deploy: add:",
      "",
      "      deploy:",
      "        requires:",
      "          - test",
      "        filters:",
      "          tags:",
      "            only: /^beta-.*$/",
      "",
      "This causes deploy to run only for tags starting with \"beta-\" (e.g. \"beta-main-0.1.1\"). Branch commits and tags starting with \"alpha-\" will not match and thus will not run the deploy job. If you need a different stricter pattern (for example ensuring semantic versioning after the name), you can adjust the regex accordingly (e.g. /^beta-[^-]+-\\d+\\.\\d+\\.\\d+$/)."
    ],
    "ActualAnswer": [
